## Modeling (binding decisions)
- NECESSITY-DIRECTION encoding: (permitted ∧ role ∧ action) => module ∈
  allowed set. Wrong-positive advice ("you CAN do X") is formally INVALID;
  over-restrictive advice ("you cannot do X" when you can) deliberately
  passes — the safe direction. READ claims not validated.
- SoD scenarios modeled as PermAction ENUM VALUES (APPROVE_OWN_WORK,
  AUDIT_OWN_WRITE_SCOPE, INVESTIGATE_OWN_AREA) => (not permitted) — NOT as
  free BOOLs. Round-1 evidence: 5 free scenario booleans → 0/6 test cases
  conclusive (all TRANSLATION_AMBIGUOUS); collapsing to enum values
  restored INVALID/VALID verdicts. New API lesson recorded: rule ids min
  12 chars; single-argument (or …) rejected.
- ProcessOwner row-level assignment + PartnerConsultant delegation BOOLs
  DROPPED after ambiguity testing — claims about those roles ride the
  AMBIGUOUS→HITL fail-safe; role-value descriptions still inform the
  translator. SCOPING DECISION for owner.
Final: types Role(12)/PermAction(7)/Module(14); 4 variables; 24 rules.

